# APReview runner crontab. Master copy; edit here then re-run:
#   crontab $HOME/review/etc/crontab.reviewprs
# Inspect with:  crontab -l          Disable with: crontab -r
#
# Times are the runner's local time. Everything is serialised on one flock, so
# an overrunning job makes the next slot log "SKIPPED" rather than pile up.
SHELL=/bin/bash
MAILTO=""
# No PATH is set here on purpose: cron does not expand variables in these lines,
# so any value would hardcode one machine's layout. Every script below sources
# review-env.sh first, which puts the toolchain, ccache and the npm-global bin
# (claude, codex) on PATH for everything it runs.

# Base clones refreshed nightly, well clear of the review slots.
30 2 * * *   $HOME/review/bin/refresh-repos.sh

# Follow-ups: frequent and cheap. Does nothing when nothing has moved.
# Waits up to 30m for the lock: a followup slot falls 34m after an `all` slot,
# so a long `all` run (34-71m observed) would otherwise skip the next followup
# every time. 30m rescues that without letting slots pile up: the next followup
# is 3h away regardless.
47 1,4,7,10,13,16,19,22 * * *   REVIEWPRS_LOCK_WAIT=1800 $HOME/review/bin/run-reviewprs.sh followup

# The full label sweep, every 6 hours.
13 0,6,12,18 * * *   $HOME/review/bin/run-reviewprs.sh all

# A separate project, reviewed once a day. It waits up to 2h for the lock rather
# than skipping: a once-a-day job that loses the race does not run at all that day.
25 5 * * *   REVIEWPRS_LOCK_WAIT=7200 $HOME/review/bin/run-reviewprs.sh rsync

# Backstop reaper: catches anything a run left behind that its own exit trap
# missed (e.g. a run killed outright). No-ops while a run is active.
50 * * * *   $HOME/review/bin/reap-orphans.sh >> $HOME/review/logs/reap.log 2>&1

# Sample Claude's real usage meter hourly, so the dashboard has a trace even
# across stretches with no runs. `claude -p /usage` reports the true session and
# weekly percentages headlessly - no calibration needed.
35 * * * *   $HOME/review/bin/claude-usage-probe.sh hourly

# HANDOVER, 2026-09-16 to 2026-09-30. Commenting moved to the AP-Review bot, but
# only a comment's author may edit it, so the bot cannot collapse the reviews the
# previous account left behind. This job does that one edit as the old account,
# using the box's own gh login rather than the bot token. It no-ops after
# REVIEW_DEPRECATE_UNTIL, so a forgotten line costs nothing - but delete it then,
# because after that date the bot is the only account this box needs.
20 * * * *   $HOME/review/bin/deprecate-legacy-comments.sh >> $HOME/review/logs/deprecate.log 2>&1

# Keep the runs dashboard current even when no run has fired recently. It is
# published to $REVIEW_PUBLIC_URL/DevCallReviews/runs.html
*/10 * * * *   $HOME/review/bin/publish-runs-page.sh
